- [x] Classified non-English and unclassified are reported separately —
  §2.3 prints `lang_non_english_n` (2,061) and `lang_unclassified_n` (11);
  `compute_vars.py:158-163` derives both (declared in
  `scripts/analysis/_vars_registry.py`, where 0357 moved `DOC_VARS`
  mid-review), and `tests/test_language_claims.py` pins the partition
  against total-minus-English.
- [x] Abstract and Conclusion claims match Table 3 — the four
  cross-language claims are gone (Abstract, §1 ×2, §5), guarded by
  `test_abstract_and_conclusion_claim_no_cross_language_capability` and
  `test_no_undemonstrated_claim_anywhere_in_the_document`, the second of
  which reads the file from byte zero so the title and keywords are covered
  too.
- [x] Language detection and the English-only institutional indexing stated
